 ["Forehead sparing is the fingerprint of a corticobulbar (upper motor neuron) facial palsy", "Pseudobulbar palsy needs two lesions: look for bilateral capsular or pontine strokes, or motor neuron disease", "Emotional facial movements survive corticobulbar lesions because they use a separate limbic-brainstem route"],
